From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Route 206 under the bridge: past the scenery the map goes on, not mirrored (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Past the scenery beside Route 206 the map is drawn again mirrored about
its border (0069). Under the bridge, a ridge and the grass either side of
it cross both borders: mirrored, the ridge's half and its mounds and
trees showed twice, the same either side of the border, too plainly a
mirror. There (sPortMovedRows: tiles 617 to 661 of the matrix's z on the
left, 624 to 661 on the right) the map goes on as its own other side
instead, moved over: the two borders' halves of the ridge meet. The
river, its ledges and the plateau north of the ridge stay mirrored.

The copy's lists are cut by rows too (NitroPort_Gx3dTrimListRows: each
polygon in the rows by where it starts, so the two ways share none), and
a second copy of the model, its culling as it is, has the moved rows,
cut to the strip by the other border. The props go by the same rows
(MapPropManager_RenderRows). The rows were picked a side at a time where
no gap opens where the two ways meet past the border (a cliff ending in
the open, the white behind it showing); on the right one row of the
mirror is kept under the moved ones' first for that.

